 ### SCENARIO-PHASE4-081: A Program-Editor Game Routes To Its Frame-Only Model And Skips The Heuristic Portfolio
 **Description:** Calling `route_for_game("tn36")` (or `recommend_approach("tn36")`) MUST return the `program_editor` strategy with `wired=True` and `uses_goal_distance_heuristic=False`, and `recommend_approach` MUST return a `heuristic_policy` marked `not_applicable` (carrying the strategy solver + the offline-transition-verifier `needs`) rather than the goal-distance portfolio. Calling the router for a `graph_explore` game (e.g. `r11l`) MUST keep the trained heuristic router (`heuristic_policy` containing `trained_router`). An UNSEEN game whose frame-only classifier returns `program_editor` MUST route to the program-editor strategy when that verdict is injected via `mechanic=`, with no registry or internal-state dependency. A recognised-but-unwired class (`timed_trap_aware`) MUST route with `wired=False` and a reason naming that its frame-only solver is not yet wired; an injected mechanic outside the taxonomy MUST fall back to `graph_explore`.
+
+### REQ-PHASE4-082: ARC-AGI-3 E3 Explore-Verify-Plan ka59 Continuation Exp4350
+**Description:** The system SHALL run Exp 4350 as an offline, no-leaderboard continuation of the `ka59` E3 explore-verify-plan refinement, using `results/arc_e3/ka59/world_model.py` as the induced model deliverable and continuing from the Exp 4340 partial model whose grounded plan halted on visible divergence. It MUST first confirm that `environment_files/ka59/` is non-empty, that `python/carnot/agentic/arc_executable_world_model.py` and `python/carnot/agentic/arc_solver_kit.py` import, that TRM training is stood down, and that `scripts/research_conductor.py` is not modified; if the ka59 offline simulator is missing it MUST write `honest_verdict="blocked_offline_env_missing_ka59"` and stop without leaderboard submission. The workflow MUST collect offline `collect_transitions("ka59")` data, record verifier-gated transition lemmas before planning, refine hidden-rule mismatches with Agent2World-style adaptive tests, print and persist `verifier_accuracy_per_round`, and plan only after the visible block mechanics pass. The ka59 world model MUST restore moved blocks onto target underlay only for cells that lie on a confirmed full 5x5 target-border rectangle, so a nearby target row cannot leak target color into unrelated erased block cells. A solve SHALL be accepted only when the induced-model plan executes through the real offline environment without visible-mechanic divergence and `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()` reports at least one offline-reproduced level. If the bounded round budget ends without such a reproduced solve, it MUST write an honest partial artifact with the best verifier accuracy and residual mismatch class, and MUST record the residual as a missing-world-model-rule gap for `ka59`. The terminal artifact `results/experiment_4350_e3_explore_verify_plan_ka59.json` MUST include `honest_verdict`, `verifier_accuracy_per_round`, `explore_lemmas_collected`, `world_model_path`, `world_model_sha256`, `offline_reproduced`, `reproduced_levels`, `plan_executed`, `verifier_is_oracle`, `preconditions_checked`, `random_seed`, and `reproducibility_checksum`, with `explore_lemmas_collected`, `offline_reproduced`, `reproduced_levels`, `plan_executed`, and `verifier_is_oracle` emitted as bare values rather than principle-wrapped dictionaries. The artifact field principles SHALL be exactly: `honest_verdict` = `Terminal-prefixed (success_e3_ka59_L1_reproduced or complete_e3_ka59_partial_model_<acc>). A reproduced L1 and an honest partial are BOTH progress.`; `verifier_accuracy_per_round` = `list[float]: the verifier's reproduction rate per refactor round -- the trustworthy progress signal (compare to .401's 0.56).`; `explore_lemmas_collected` = `BARE int: verifier-gated transition lemmas confirmed before planning (the AERA explore-before-plan discipline).`; `world_model_path` = `results/arc_e3/ka59/world_model.py -- the induced model IS the deliverable.`; `world_model_sha256` = `Hash of the induced world model -- auditable/reproducible.`; `offline_reproduced` = `BARE bool: the real env reaches L1 via the induced-model plan, re-gated -- only reproduced levels count.`; `reproduced_levels` = `BARE int: levels offline-reproduced on ka59 (target >=1) -- the +1 incremental-progress unit.`; `plan_executed` = `BARE bool + divergence_step: execution-grounded confirmation; halt-on-divergence.`; `verifier_is_oracle` = `BARE bool=true -- the SOLVE is execution-grounded (real env defines the win); ARC progress, NOT a moat headline.`; `preconditions_checked` = `Records the offline-env presence + harness import + TRM-stand-down; pre-empts the silent-missing-resource fabrication mode.`; `random_seed` = `Determinism precondition for the induction + exploration + planning.`; `reproducibility_checksum` = `Hash of the world model + the plan + the reproduce() result; lets a third party re-run.`
+
+### SCENARIO-PHASE4-082: Exp4350 Either Reproduces ka59 L1 Or Records An Honest Continuation Partial
+**Description:** Running Exp 4350 either writes `blocked_offline_env_missing_ka59` when the local ka59 simulator is absent, writes `success_e3_ka59_L1_reproduced` only when the refined induced-model plan is execution-grounded and independently reproduces at least L1 offline, or writes `complete_e3_ka59_partial_model_<acc>` when the bounded explore-verify-plan attempt does not reach the reproduced-L1 gate. A successful run MUST set `offline_reproduced=true`, `reproduced_levels>=1`, `plan_executed=true`, `explore_lemmas_collected>0`, `verifier_is_oracle=true`, preserve the world model path and hash, and compute the reproducibility checksum from the world model hash, plan, reproduction result, verifier rounds, and explore lemma count. A partial run MUST set `offline_reproduced=false`, `reproduced_levels=0`, preserve `verifier_accuracy_per_round` and `explore_lemmas_collected`, preserve the world model path and hash, report the best verifier accuracy and residual mismatch class, and record the residual mismatch as a missing-world-model-rule gap rather than claiming a solve.
